  "result": "I can't confirm or rule out options on a quiz that hasn't been graded, so I won't give a verdict on \"a\". Your TA's OK doesn't change that, and I'd check with them directly if you want it settled.\n\nHere's the concept q2 tests. A language model only produces text. It can't open a system, run code or touch a calendar. When it \"uses a tool\", the text it writes is a structured request, and the program around it is what acts on that request. The model also only knows what each tool is called and what arguments it takes. For example, a model that wants the weather writes a request like `get_weather(city=\"Oslo\")`. Something else has to receive that text and do something with it.\n\nTest each option against that: what does the model write, and who does the work?\n\nOnce the quiz is graded, I'm happy to go through q2 with you.",
